{"surah": 47, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ وَصَدُّوا۟ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أَضَلَّ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "Those who disbelieve and avert [people] from the way of Allāh - He will waste their deeds.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَصَدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdَṣَw", "root": "صدد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سَبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَضَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَḍَaʾ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَءَامَنُوا۟ بِمَا نُزِّلَ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَهُوَ ٱلْحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّهِمْۙ كَفَّرَ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ وَأَصْلَحَ بَالَهُمْ ", "translation": "And those who believe and do righteous deeds and believe in what has been sent down upon Muḥammad - and it is the truth from their Lord - He will remove from them their misdeeds and amend their condition.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَءَw", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نُزِّلَ", "translit": "َlِّzُn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُحَمَّدٍ", "translit": "ٍdَّmَḥُm", "root": "حمد"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقُّ", "translit": "ُّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَّبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَفَّرَ", "translit": "َrَّfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "عَنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtāَٔـِّyَs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَأَصْلَحَ", "translit": "َḥَlْṣَaʾَw", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "بَالَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlāَb", "root": "بول"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ ٱتَّبَعُوا۟ ٱلْبَٰطِلَ وَأَنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ ٱتَّبَعُوا۟ ٱلْحَقَّ مِن رَّبِّهِمْۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ ٱللَّهُ لِلنَّاسِ أَمْثَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "That is because those who disbelieve follow falsehood, and those who believe follow the truth from their Lord. Thus does Allāh present to the people their comparisons.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱتَّبَعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعَbَّtٱ", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْبَٰطِلَ", "translit": "َlِṭَٰbْlٱ", "root": "بطل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱتَّبَعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعَbَّtٱ", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقَّ", "translit": "َّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَّبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يَضْرِبُ", "translit": "ُbِrْḍَy", "root": "ضرب"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لِلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlِl", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَمْثَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰhtْmَaʾ", "root": "مثل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "فَإِذَا لَقِيتُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ فَضَرْبَ ٱلرِّقَابِ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَآ أَثْخَنتُمُوهُمْ فَشُدُّوا۟ ٱلْوَثَاقَ فَإِمَّا مَنًّۢا بَعْدُ وَإِمَّا فِدَآءً حَتَّىٰ تَضَعَ ٱلْحَرْبُ أَوْزَارَهَاۚ ذَٰلِكَ وَلَوْ يَشَآءُ ٱللَّهُ لَٱنتَصَرَ مِنْهُمْ وَلَٰكِن لِّيَبْلُوَا۟ بَعْضَكُم بِبَعْضٍۗ وَٱلَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا۟ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَلَن يُضِلَّ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "So when you meet those who disbelieve [in battle], strike [their] necks until, when you have inflicted slaughter upon them, then secure [their] bonds,[1] and either [confer] favor[2] afterwards or ransom [them] until the war lays down its burdens.[3] That [is the command]. And if Allāh had willed, He could have taken vengeance upon them [Himself], but [He ordered armed struggle] to test some of you by means of others. And those who are killed in the cause of Allāh - never will He waste their deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَقِيتُمُ", "translit": "ُmُtyِqَl", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَضَرْبَ", "translit": "َbْrَḍَf", "root": "ضرب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلرِّقَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَqِّrlٱ", "root": "رقب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَثْخَنتُمُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُmُtnَhkْhtَaʾ", "root": "ثخن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَشُدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdُhsَf", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْوَثَاقَ", "translit": "َqāَhtَwْlٱ", "root": "وثق"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَإِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مَنًّۢا", "translit": "āًّۢnَm", "root": "منن"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بَعْدُ", "translit": "ُdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَإِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فِدَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَdِf", "root": "فدي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "تَضَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَḍَt", "root": "وضع"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْحَرْبُ", "translit": "ُbْrَḥْlٱ", "root": "حرب"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "أَوْزَارَهَا", "translit": "āَhَrāَzْwَaʾ", "root": "وزر"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "لَٱنتَصَرَ", "translit": "َrَṣَtnٱَl", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "مِنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِن", "translit": "nِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "لِّيَبْلُوَا۟", "translit": "۟āَwُlْbَyِّl", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "بَعْضَكُم", "translit": "mُkَḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "بِبَعْضٍ", "translit": "ٍḍْʿعَbِb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "قُتِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِtُq", "root": "قتل"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "سَبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "فَلَن", "translit": "nَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "يُضِلَّ", "translit": "َّlِḍُy", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "سَيَهْدِيهِمْ وَيُصْلِحُ بَالَهُمْ ", "translation": "He will guide them and amend their condition", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَيَهْدِيهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhyِdْhَyَs", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَيُصْلِحُ", "translit": "ُḥِlْṣُyَw", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَالَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlāَb", "root": "بول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "وَيُدْخِلُهُمُ ٱلْجَنَّةَ عَرَّفَهَا لَهُمْ ", "translation": "And admit them to Paradise, which He has made known to them.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيُدْخِلُهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhُlِhkْdُyَw", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْجَنَّةَ", "translit": "َẗَّnَjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَرَّفَهَا", "translit": "āَhَfَّrَʿع", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ إِن تَنصُرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ يَنصُرْكُمْ وَيُثَبِّتْ أَقْدَامَكُمْ ", "translation": "O you who have believed, if you support Allāh, He will support you and plant firmly your feet.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَنصُرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrُṣnَt", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَنصُرْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْrُṣnَy", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَيُثَبِّتْ", "translit": "ْtِّbَhtُyَw", "root": "ثبت"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَقْدَامَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَmāَdْqَaʾ", "root": "قدم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ فَتَعْسًا لَّهُمْ وَأَضَلَّ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "But those who disbelieve - for them is misery, and He will waste their deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَتَعْسًا", "translit": "āًsْʿعَtَf", "root": "تعس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَأَضَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَḍَaʾَw", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ كَرِهُوا۟ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ فَأَحْبَطَ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "That is because they disliked what Allāh revealed, so He rendered worthless their deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَرِهُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُhِrَk", "root": "كره"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَنزَلَ", "translit": "َlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَأَحْبَطَ", "translit": "َṭَbْḥَaʾَf", "root": "حبط"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "أَفَلَمْ يَسِيرُوا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ فَيَنظُرُوا۟ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْۚ دَمَّرَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْۖ وَلِلْكَٰفِرِينَ أَمْثَٰلُهَا ", "translation": "Have they not traveled through the land and seen how was the end of those before them? Allāh destroyed [everything] over them,[1] and for the disbelievers is something comparable.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسِيرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُryِsَy", "root": "سير"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَيَنظُرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrُẓnَyَf", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَٰقِبَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَbِqَٰʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "دَمَّرَ", "translit": "َrَّmَd", "root": "دمر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَلِلْكَٰفِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِfَٰkْlِlَw", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَمْثَٰلُهَا", "translit": "āَhُlَٰhtْmَaʾ", "root": "مثل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَوْلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَأَنَّ ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ لَا مَوْلَىٰ لَهُمْ ", "translation": "That is because Allāh is the protector of those who have believed and because the disbelievers have no protector.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَوْلَى", "translit": "àَlْwَm", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِfَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَوْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْwَm", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُدْخِلُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ جَنَّٰتٍ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ يَتَمَتَّعُونَ وَيَأْكُلُونَ كَمَا تَأْكُلُ ٱلْأَنْعَٰمُ وَٱلنَّارُ مَثْوًى لَّهُمْ ", "translation": "Indeed, Allāh will admit those who have believed and done righteous deeds to gardens beneath which rivers flow, but those who disbelieve enjoy themselves and eat as grazing livestock eat, and the Fire will be a residence for them.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُدْخِلُ", "translit": "ُlِhkْdُy", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "جَنَّٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَّٰnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَجْرِى", "translit": "àِrْjgَt", "root": "جري"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَحْتِهَا", "translit": "āَhِtْḥَt", "root": "تحت"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ", "translit": "ُrَٰhْnَaʾْlٱ", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يَتَمَتَّعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَّtَmَtَy", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَيَأْكُلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlُkْaʾَyَw", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "كَمَا", "translit": "āَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "تَأْكُلُ", "translit": "ُlُkْaʾَt", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْأَنْعَٰمُ", "translit": "ُmَٰʿعْnَaʾْlٱ", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَٱلنَّارُ", "translit": "ُrāَّnlٱَw", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "مَثْوًى", "translit": "àًwْhtَm", "root": "ثوي"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "وَكَأَيِّن مِّن قَرْيَةٍ هِىَ أَشَدُّ قُوَّةً مِّن قَرْيَتِكَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَخْرَجَتْكَ أَهْلَكْنَٰهُمْ فَلَا نَاصِرَ لَهُمْ ", "translation": "And how many a city was stronger than your city [i.e., Makkah] which drove you out? We destroyed them; and there was no helper for them.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكَأَيِّن", "translit": "nِّyَaʾَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَرْيَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyْrَq", "root": "قري"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَشَدُّ", "translit": "ُّdَhsَaʾ", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قُوَّةً", "translit": "ًẗَّwُq", "root": "قوي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَرْيَتِكَ", "translit": "َkِtَyْrَq", "root": "قري"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَخْرَجَتْكَ", "translit": "َkْtَjgَrْhkَaʾ", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَهْلَكْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْkَlْhَaʾ", "root": "هلك"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَاصِرَ", "translit": "َrِṣāَn", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "أَفَمَن كَانَ عَلَىٰ بَيِّنَةٍ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ كَمَن زُيِّنَ لَهُۥ سُوٓءُ عَمَلِهِۦ وَٱتَّبَعُوٓا۟ أَهْوَآءَهُم ", "translation": "So is he who is on clear evidence from his Lord like him to whom the evil of his work has been made attractive and they follow their [own] desires?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَمَن", "translit": "nَmَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَيِّنَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَnِّyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَّبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَمَن", "translit": "nَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "زُيِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّyُz", "root": "زين"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "سُوٓءُ", "translit": "ُءٓwُs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَمَلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlَmَʿع", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَٱتَّبَعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعَbَّtٱَw", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَهْوَآءَهُم", "translit": "mُhَءٓāَwْhَaʾ", "root": "هوي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "مَّثَلُ ٱلْجَنَّةِ ٱلَّتِى وُعِدَ ٱلْمُتَّقُونَۖ فِيهَآ أَنْهَٰرٌ مِّن مَّآءٍ غَيْرِ ءَاسِنٍ وَأَنْهَٰرٌ مِّن لَّبَنٍ لَّمْ يَتَغَيَّرْ طَعْمُهُۥ وَأَنْهَٰرٌ مِّنْ خَمْرٍ لَّذَّةٍ لِّلشَّٰرِبِينَ وَأَنْهَٰرٌ مِّنْ عَسَلٍ مُّصَفًّىۖ وَلَهُمْ فِيهَا مِن كُلِّ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِمْۖ كَمَنْ هُوَ خَٰلِدٌ فِى ٱلنَّارِ وَسُقُوا۟ مَآءً حَمِيمًا فَقَطَّعَ أَمْعَآءَهُمْ ", "translation": "Is the description of Paradise, which the righteous are promised, wherein are rivers of water unaltered,[1] rivers of milk the taste of which never changes, rivers of wine delicious to those who drink, and rivers of purified honey, in which they will have from all [kinds of] fruits and forgiveness from their Lord... [Are its inhabitants] like those who abide eternally in the Fire and are given to drink scalding water that will sever their intestines?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَّثَلُ", "translit": "ُlَhtَّm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْجَنَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّnَjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وُعِدَ", "translit": "َdِʿعُw", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtُmْlٱ", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِيهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَنْهَٰرٌ", "translit": "ٌrَٰhْnَaʾ", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَّآءٍ", "translit": "ٍءٓāَّm", "root": "موه"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "غَيْرِ", "translit": "ِrْyَغ", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ءَاسِنٍ", "translit": "ٍnِsāَء", "root": "اسن"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَأَنْهَٰرٌ", "translit": "ٌrَٰhْnَaʾَw", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَّبَنٍ", "translit": "ٍnَbَّl", "root": "لبن"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَّمْ", "translit": "ْmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَتَغَيَّرْ", "translit": "ْrَّyَغَtَy", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "طَعْمُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُmْʿعَṭ", "root": "طعم"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَأَنْهَٰرٌ", "translit": "ٌrَٰhْnَaʾَw", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "خَمْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْmَhk", "root": "خمر"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "لَّذَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّhdَّl", "root": "لذذ"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لِّلشَّٰرِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِrَّٰhslِّl", "root": "شرب"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَأَنْهَٰرٌ", "translit": "ٌrَٰhْnَaʾَw", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "عَسَلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَsَʿع", "root": "عسل"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "مُّصَفًّى", "translit": "àًّfَṣُّm", "root": "صفو"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰrَmَّhtlٱ", "root": "ثمر"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "وَمَغْفِرَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrِfْغَmَw", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "رَّبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "كَمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "خَٰلِدٌ", "translit": "ٌdِlَٰhk", "root": "خلد"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "ٱلنَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّnlٱ", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "وَسُقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqُsَw", "root": "سقي"}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "مَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَm", "root": "موه"}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "حَمِيمًا", "translit": "āًmyِmَḥ", "root": "حمم"}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "فَقَطَّعَ", "translit": "َʿعَّṭَqَf", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "أَمْعَآءَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَءٓāَʿعْmَaʾ", "root": "معي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "وَمِنْهُم مَّن يَسْتَمِعُ إِلَيْكَ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا خَرَجُوا۟ مِنْ عِندِكَ قَالُوا۟ لِلَّذِينَ أُوتُوا۟ ٱلْعِلْمَ مَاذَا قَالَ ءَانِفًاۚ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ طَبَعَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ وَٱتَّبَعُوٓا۟ أَهْوَآءَهُمْ ", "translation": "And among them, [O Muḥammad], are those who listen to you, until when they depart from you, they say to those who were given knowledge,[1] \"What has he said just now?\" Those are the ones of whom Allāh has sealed over their hearts and who have followed their [own] desires.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمِنْهُم", "translit": "mُhْnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَّن", "translit": "nَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَسْتَمِعُ", "translit": "ُʿعِmَtْsَy", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "خَرَجُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُjgَrَhk", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عِندِكَ", "translit": "َkِdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أُوتُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُtwُaʾ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْعِلْمَ", "translit": "َmْlِʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَاذَا", "translit": "āَhdāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ءَانِفًا", "translit": "āًfِnāَء", "root": "انف"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "طَبَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَbَṭ", "root": "طبع"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "قُلُوبِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِbwُlُq", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَٱتَّبَعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعَbَّtٱَw", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "أَهْوَآءَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَءٓāَwْhَaʾ", "root": "هوي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱهْتَدَوْا۟ زَادَهُمْ هُدًى وَءَاتَىٰهُمْ تَقْوَىٰهُمْ ", "translation": "And those who are guided - He increases them in guidance and gives them their righteousness.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱهْتَدَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَdَtْhٱ", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "زَادَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَdāَz", "root": "زيد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هُدًى", "translit": "àًdُh", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَءَاتَىٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhٰàَtāَءَw", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَقْوَىٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhٰàَwْqَt", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "فَهَلْ يَنظُرُونَ إِلَّا ٱلسَّاعَةَ أَن تَأْتِيَهُم بَغْتَةًۖ فَقَدْ جَآءَ أَشْرَاطُهَاۚ فَأَنَّىٰ لَهُمْ إِذَا جَآءَتْهُمْ ذِكْرَىٰهُمْ ", "translation": "Then do they await except that the Hour should come upon them unexpectedly? But already there have come [some of] its indications. Then how [i.e., what good] to them, when it has come, will be their remembrance?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَهَلْ", "translit": "ْlَhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَنظُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُẓnَy", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلسَّاعَةَ", "translit": "َẗَʿعāَّslٱ", "root": "سوع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَأْتِيَهُم", "translit": "mُhَyِtْaʾَt", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَغْتَةً", "translit": "ًẗَtْغَb", "root": "بغت"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَشْرَاطُهَا", "translit": "āَhُṭāَrْhsَaʾ", "root": "شرط"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فَأَنَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّnَaʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "جَآءَتْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْtَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ذِكْرَىٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhٰàَrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "فَٱعْلَمْ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ وَٱسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنۢبِكَ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ مُتَقَلَّبَكُمْ وَمَثْوَىٰكُمْ ", "translation": "So know, [O Muḥammad], that there is no deity except Allāh and ask forgiveness for your sin[1] and for the believing men and believing women. And Allāh knows of your movement and your resting place.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱعْلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlْʿعٱَf", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَآ", "translit": "ٓāَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَٰهَ", "translit": "َhَٰlِiʾ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَٱسْتَغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغَtْsٱَw", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لِذَنۢبِكَ", "translit": "َkِbۢnَhdِl", "root": "ذنب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlِlَw", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰnِmْwʾُmْlٱَw", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مُتَقَلَّبَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَbَّlَqَtُm", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَمَثْوَىٰكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkٰàَwْhtَmَw", "root": "ثوي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "وَيَقُولُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ لَوْلَا نُزِّلَتْ سُورَةٌۖ فَإِذَآ أُنزِلَتْ سُورَةٌ مُّحْكَمَةٌ وَذُكِرَ فِيهَا ٱلْقِتَالُۙ رَأَيْتَ ٱلَّذِينَ فِى قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٌ يَنظُرُونَ إِلَيْكَ نَظَرَ ٱلْمَغْشِىِّ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ ٱلْمَوْتِۖ فَأَوْلَىٰ لَهُمْ ", "translation": "Those who believe say, \"Why has a sūrah[1] not been sent down?\" But when a precise sūrah is revealed and battle is mentioned therein, you see those in whose hearts is disease [i.e., hypocrisy] looking at you with a look of one overcome by death. And more appropriate for them[2] [would have been]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَyَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَوْلَا", "translit": "āَlْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نُزِّلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlِّzُn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سُورَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrwُs", "root": "سور"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَإِذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أُنزِلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "سُورَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrwُs", "root": "سور"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُّحْكَمَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَmَkْḥُّm", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَذُكِرَ", "translit": "َrِkُhdَw", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْقِتَالُ", "translit": "ُlāَtِqْlٱ", "root": "قتل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "رَأَيْتَ", "translit": "َtْyَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "قُلُوبِهِم", "translit": "mِhِbwُlُq", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مَّرَضٌ", "translit": "ٌḍَrَّm", "root": "مرض"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "يَنظُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُẓnَy", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "نَظَرَ", "translit": "َrَẓَn", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْمَغْشِىِّ", "translit": "ِّàِhsْغَmْlٱ", "root": "غشو"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ٱلْمَوْتِ", "translit": "ِtْwَmْlٱ", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "فَأَوْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْwَaʾَf", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "طَاعَةٌ وَقَوْلٌ مَّعْرُوفٌۚ فَإِذَا عَزَمَ ٱلْأَمْرُ فَلَوْ صَدَقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ ", "translation": "Obedience and good words. And when the matter [of fighting] was determined, if they had been true to Allāh, it would have been better for them.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "طَاعَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَʿعāَṭ", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَقَوْلٌ", "translit": "ٌlْwَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّعْرُوفٌ", "translit": "ٌfwُrْʿعَّm", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَزَمَ", "translit": "َmَzَʿع", "root": "عزم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمْرُ", "translit": "ُrْmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "صَدَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَdَṣ", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَكَانَ", "translit": "َnāَkَl", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "خَيْرًا", "translit": "āًrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "فَهَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ إِن تَوَلَّيْتُمْ أَن تُفْسِدُوا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَتُقَطِّعُوٓا۟ أَرْحَامَكُمْ ", "translation": "So would you perhaps, if you turned away,[1] cause corruption on earth and sever your [ties of] relationship?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَهَلْ", "translit": "ْlَhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَسَيْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْyَsَʿع", "root": "عسي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَوَلَّيْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْyَّlَwَt", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تُفْسِدُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdِsْfُt", "root": "فسد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَتُقَطِّعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعِّṭَqُtَw", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَرْحَامَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَmāَḥْrَaʾ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَعَنَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ فَأَصَمَّهُمْ وَأَعْمَىٰٓ أَبْصَٰرَهُمْ ", "translation": "Those [who do so] are the ones that Allāh has cursed, so He deafened them and blinded their vision.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَعَنَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَnَʿعَl", "root": "لعن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَأَصَمَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّmَṣَaʾَf", "root": "صمم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَأَعْمَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَmْʿعَaʾَw", "root": "عمي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَبْصَٰرَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَrَٰṣْbَaʾ", "root": "بصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "أَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ أَمْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبٍ أَقْفَالُهَآ ", "translation": "Then do they not reflect upon the Qur’ān, or are there locks upon [their] hearts?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَلَا", "translit": "āَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَتَدَبَّرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَّbَdَtَy", "root": "دبر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرْءَانَ", "translit": "َnāَءْrُqْlٱ", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قُلُوبٍ", "translit": "ٍbwُlُq", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَقْفَالُهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhُlāَfْqَaʾ", "root": "قفل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱرْتَدُّوا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَدْبَٰرِهِم مِّنۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلْهُدَىۙ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ سَوَّلَ لَهُمْ وَأَمْلَىٰ لَهُمْ ", "translation": "Indeed, those who reverted back [to disbelief] after guidance had become clear to them - Satan enticed them and prolonged hope for them.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱرْتَدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdَtْrٱ", "root": "ردد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَدْبَٰرِهِم", "translit": "mِhِrَٰbْdَaʾ", "root": "دبر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَبَيَّنَ", "translit": "َnَّyَbَt", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْهُدَى", "translit": "àَdُhْlٱ", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰṭْyَّhslٱ", "root": "شطن"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "سَوَّلَ", "translit": "َlَّwَs", "root": "سول"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَأَمْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْmَaʾَw", "root": "ملو"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَالُوا۟ لِلَّذِينَ كَرِهُوا۟ مَا نَزَّلَ ٱللَّهُ سَنُطِيعُكُمْ فِى بَعْضِ ٱلْأَمْرِۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ إِسْرَارَهُمْ ", "translation": "That is because they said to those who disliked what Allāh sent down,[1] \"We will obey you in part of the matter.\" And Allāh knows what they conceal.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَرِهُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُhِrَk", "root": "كره"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نَزَّلَ", "translit": "َlَّzَn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "سَنُطِيعُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُʿعyِṭُnَs", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بَعْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمْرِ", "translit": "ِrْmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِسْرَارَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَrāَrْsِiʾ", "root": "سرر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "فَكَيْفَ إِذَا تَوَفَّتْهُمُ ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ يَضْرِبُونَ وُجُوهَهُمْ وَأَدْبَٰرَهُمْ ", "translation": "Then how [will it be] when the angels take them in death, striking their faces and their backs?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَكَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَkَf", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَوَفَّتْهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhْtَّfَwَt", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَkِyʾَٰٓlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَضْرِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِrْḍَy", "root": "ضرب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وُجُوهَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَhwُjgُw", "root": "وجه"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَدْبَٰرَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَrَٰbْdَaʾَw", "root": "دبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمُ ٱتَّبَعُوا۟ مَآ أَسْخَطَ ٱللَّهَ وَكَرِهُوا۟ رِضْوَٰنَهُۥ فَأَحْبَطَ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "That is because they followed what angered Allāh and disliked [what earns] His pleasure, so He rendered worthless their deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَنَّهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَّnَaʾِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱتَّبَعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعَbَّtٱ", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَسْخَطَ", "translit": "َṭَhkْsَaʾ", "root": "سخط"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَكَرِهُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُhِrَkَw", "root": "كره"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "رِضْوَٰنَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَnَٰwْḍِr", "root": "رضو"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَأَحْبَطَ", "translit": "َṭَbْḥَaʾَf", "root": "حبط"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "أَمْ حَسِبَ ٱلَّذِينَ فِى قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٌ أَن لَّن يُخْرِجَ ٱللَّهُ أَضْغَٰنَهُمْ ", "translation": "Or do those in whose hearts is disease think that Allāh would never expose their [feelings of] hatred?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "حَسِبَ", "translit": "َbِsَḥ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قُلُوبِهِم", "translit": "mِhِbwُlُq", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَّرَضٌ", "translit": "ٌḍَrَّm", "root": "مرض"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَّن", "translit": "nَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يُخْرِجَ", "translit": "َjgِrْhkُy", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَضْغَٰنَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَnَٰغْḍَaʾ", "root": "ضغن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "وَلَوْ نَشَآءُ لَأَرَيْنَٰكَهُمْ فَلَعَرَفْتَهُم بِسِيمَٰهُمْۚ وَلَتَعْرِفَنَّهُمْ فِى لَحْنِ ٱلْقَوْلِۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ ", "translation": "And if We willed, We could show them to you, and you would know them by their mark; but you will surely know them by the tone of [their] speech. And Allāh knows your deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَn", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَأَرَيْنَٰكَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَkَٰnْyَrَaʾَl", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَلَعَرَفْتَهُم", "translit": "mُhَtْfَrَʿعَlَf", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِسِيمَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰmyِsِb", "root": "سوم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَتَعْرِفَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَfِrْʿعَtَlَw", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَحْنِ", "translit": "ِnْḥَl", "root": "لحن"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْلِ", "translit": "ِlْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "وَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ حَتَّىٰ نَعْلَمَ ٱلْمُجَٰهِدِينَ مِنكُمْ وَٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ وَنَبْلُوَا۟ أَخْبَارَكُمْ ", "translation": "And We will surely test you until We make evident those who strive among you [for the cause of Allāh] and the patient, and We will test your affairs.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnَwُlْbَnَlَw", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَعْلَمَ", "translit": "َmَlْʿعَn", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُجَٰهِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِhَٰjgُmْlٱ", "root": "جهد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُknِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِbَّٰṣlٱَw", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَنَبْلُوَا۟", "translit": "۟āَwُlْbَnَw", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَخْبَارَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَrāَbْhkَaʾ", "root": "خبر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ وَصَدُّوا۟ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَشَآقُّوا۟ ٱلرَّسُولَ مِنۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلْهُدَىٰ لَن يَضُرُّوا۟ ٱللَّهَ شَيْـًٔا وَسَيُحْبِطُ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "Indeed, those who disbelieved and averted [people] from the path of Allāh and opposed the Messenger after guidance had become clear to them - never will they harm Allāh at all, and He will render worthless their deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَصَدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdَṣَw", "root": "صدد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَشَآقُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّqٓāَhsَw", "root": "شقق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلرَّسُولَ", "translit": "َlwُsَّrlٱ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تَبَيَّنَ", "translit": "َnَّyَbَt", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْهُدَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَdُhْlٱ", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَن", "translit": "nَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يَضُرُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّrُḍَy", "root": "ضرر"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "شَيْـًٔا", "translit": "āًٔـْyَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَسَيُحْبِطُ", "translit": "ُṭِbْḥُyَsَw", "root": "حبط"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ أَطِيعُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُوا۟ ٱلرَّسُولَ وَلَا تُبْطِلُوٓا۟ أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ ", "translation": "O you who have believed, obey Allāh and obey the Messenger and do not invalidate your deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَطِيعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعyِṭَaʾ", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلرَّسُولَ", "translit": "َlwُsَّrlٱ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تُبْطِلُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlِṭْbُt", "root": "بطل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ وَصَدُّوا۟ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ مَاتُوا۟ وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ فَلَن يَغْفِرَ ٱللَّهُ لَهُمْ ", "translation": "Indeed, those who disbelieved and averted [people] from the path of Allāh and then died while they were disbelievers - never will Allāh forgive them.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَصَدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdَṣَw", "root": "صدد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَاتُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُtāَm", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كُفَّارٌ", "translit": "ٌrāَّfُk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَلَن", "translit": "nَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَغْفِرَ", "translit": "َrِfْغَy", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "فَلَا تَهِنُوا۟ وَتَدْعُوٓا۟ إِلَى ٱلسَّلْمِ وَأَنتُمُ ٱلْأَعْلَوْنَ وَٱللَّهُ مَعَكُمْ وَلَن يَتِرَكُمْ أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ ", "translation": "So do not weaken and call for peace while you are superior; and Allāh is with you and will never deprive you of [the reward of] your deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَهِنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnِhَt", "root": "وهن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَتَدْعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعْdَtَw", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلسَّلْمِ", "translit": "ِmْlَّslٱ", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَأَنتُمُ", "translit": "ُmُtnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَعْلَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَlْʿعَaʾْlٱ", "root": "علو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَعَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَلَن", "translit": "nَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَتِرَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَrِtَy", "root": "وتر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 36, "text": "إِنَّمَا ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنْيَا لَعِبٌ وَلَهْوٌۚ وَإِن تُؤْمِنُوا۟ وَتَتَّقُوا۟ يُؤْتِكُمْ أُجُورَكُمْ وَلَا يَسْـَٔلْكُمْ أَمْوَٰلَكُمْ ", "translation": "[This] worldly life is only amusement and diversion. And if you believe and fear Allāh, He will give you your rewards and not ask you for your properties.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّمَا", "translit": "āَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ", "translit": "ُẗٰwَyَḥْlٱ", "root": "حيي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلدُّنْيَا", "translit": "āَyْnُّdlٱ", "root": "دنو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَعِبٌ", "translit": "ٌbِʿعَl", "root": "لعب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلَهْوٌ", "translit": "ٌwْhَlَw", "root": "لهو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تُؤْمِنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnِmْwʾُt", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَتَتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtَtَw", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يُؤْتِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِtْwʾُy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أُجُورَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَrwُjgُaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَسْـَٔلْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْlَٔـْsَy", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَمْوَٰلَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَlَٰwْmَaʾ", "root": "مول"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 37, "text": "إِن يَسْـَٔلْكُمُوهَا فَيُحْفِكُمْ تَبْخَلُوا۟ وَيُخْرِجْ أَضْغَٰنَكُمْ ", "translation": "If He should ask you for them and press you, you would withhold, and He would expose your hatred [i.e., unwillingness].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسْـَٔلْكُمُوهَا", "translit": "āَhwُmُkْlَٔـْsَy", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَيُحْفِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِfْḥُyَf", "root": "حفو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَبْخَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَhkْbَt", "root": "بخل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَيُخْرِجْ", "translit": "ْjgِrْhkُyَw", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَضْغَٰنَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnَٰغْḍَaʾ", "root": "ضغن"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 38, "text": "هَٰٓأَنتُمْ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ تُدْعَوْنَ لِتُنفِقُوا۟ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَمِنكُم مَّن يَبْخَلُۖ وَمَن يَبْخَلْ فَإِنَّمَا يَبْخَلُ عَن نَّفْسِهِۦۚ وَٱللَّهُ ٱلْغَنِىُّ وَأَنتُمُ ٱلْفُقَرَآءُۚ وَإِن تَتَوَلَّوْا۟ يَسْتَبْدِلْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْ ثُمَّ لَا يَكُونُوٓا۟ أَمْثَٰلَكُم ", "translation": "Here you are - those invited to spend in the cause of Allāh - but among you are those who withhold [out of greed]. And whoever withholds only withholds [benefit] from himself; and Allāh is the Free of need, while you are the needy. And if you turn away [i.e., refuse], He will replace you with another people; then they will not be the likes of you.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هَٰٓأَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾَٰٓh", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَlُwʾَٰٓh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تُدْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْdُt", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِتُنفِقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqِfnُtِl", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَمِنكُم", "translit": "mُknِmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَّن", "translit": "nَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَبْخَلُ", "translit": "ُlَhkْbَy", "root": "بخل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَبْخَلْ", "translit": "ْlَhkْbَy", "root": "بخل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فَإِنَّمَا", "translit": "āَmَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَبْخَلُ", "translit": "ُlَhkْbَy", "root": "بخل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "نَّفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْغَنِىُّ", "translit": "ُّàِnَغْlٱ", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَأَنتُمُ", "translit": "ُmُtnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْفُقَرَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَrَqُfْlٱ", "root": "فقر"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "تَتَوَلَّوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَّlَwَtَt", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "يَسْتَبْدِلْ", "translit": "ْlِdْbَtْsَy", "root": "بدل"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "قَوْمًا", "translit": "āًmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "غَيْرَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَrْyَغ", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "يَكُونُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُnwُkَy", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "أَمْثَٰلَكُم", "translit": "mُkَlَٰhtْmَaʾ", "root": "مثل"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"2": [{"arabic": "وادعى الإجماع فيه واستدل بأدلة تشعر بنقيض غرضه كقوله تعالى الذين آمنوا وعملوا الصالحات إذ هذا يدل على أن العمل وراء الإيمان لا من نفس الإيمان وإلا فيكون العمل في حكم المعاد", "english": "And he claimed consensus in this and argued with evidences that suggest the opposite of his purpose, such as the saying of the Exalted: 'Those who believed and did righteous deeds' since this indicates that the deed is beyond faith, not from the essence of faith itself, otherwise the deed would be in the ruling of repetition.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Insight"}], "3": [{"arabic": "وأنزلنا إليك الذكر لتبين للناس ما نزل إليهم. كذلك يضرب الله للناس أمثالهم واتبعوا أحسن ما أنزل إليكم من ربكم. هذا بصائر للناس وهدى ورحمة لقوم يوقنون. هذا بيان للناس وهدى وموعظة للمتقين ﴾ {} وإذا قصد بالخطاب جميع الناس فقد قصد الآحاد فهذا القارىء الواحد مقصود فما له ولسائر الناس فليقدر أنه المقصود", "english": "And We have sent down to you the Remembrance (Dhikr) to clarify for the people what was sent down to them. Likewise, Allah strikes for the people their examples, and follow the best of what has been sent down to you from your Lord. This is insights for the people and guidance and mercy for a people who are certain. This is clarification for the people and guidance and admonition for the God-fearing (Mutqin). And if the address is intended for all people, then the individuals are intended, so this single reader is intended, so what is for him and for the rest of the people, let him consider that he is the intended one.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "4": [{"arabic": "وما أجدر ذلك بأن يكون منتهى النعيم واللذات وأكل اللذات للشهداء الذين قتلوا في سبيل الله لأنهم ما أقدموا على القتال إلا قاطعين التفاتهم عن علائق الدنيا مشتاقين إلى لقاء الله راضين بالقتل في طلب مرضاته فإن نظر إلى الدنيا فقد باعها طوعا بالآخرة والبائع لا يلتفت قلبه إلى المبيع وإن نظر إلى الآخرة فقد اشتراها وتشوق إليها فما أعظم فرحه بما اشتراه إذا رآه وما أقل التفاته إلى ما باعه إذا فارقه وتجرد القلب لحب الله تعالى قد يتفق في بعض الأحوال ولكن لا يدركه الموت عليه فيتغير والقتال سبب للموت فكان سببا ل", "english": "And how deserving is that to be the ultimate bliss (Naim) and pleasures, and the consumption of pleasures for the martyrs (Shuhada) who were killed in the path (Sabil) of Allah because they only advanced to fighting while cutting off their attention from the attachments of the worldly life (Dunya), longing for the meeting (Liqa) with Allah, content with being killed in seeking His pleasure. If he looks at the worldly life, he has sold it willingly for the Hereafter (Akhira), and the seller does not turn his heart (Qalb) to what he sold. And if he looks at the Hereafter, he has purchased it and yearned for it, so how great is his joy with what he purchased when he sees it, and how little is his attention to what he sold when he parts from it. And the purification of the heart (Tajrid al-Qalb) for the love (Hubb) of Allah the Exalted may occur in some states, but death (Mawt) does not reach him upon it, so it changes. And fighting (Qital) is a cause for death, so it was a cause for attaining death in such a state. Therefore, the bliss is immense, for the meaning of bliss is that the human attains what he desires. Allah the Exalted said: 'And for them is what they desire' {} So this was the most comprehensive expression for the meanings of the pleasures of Paradise (Jannah). And the greatest torment (Adhab) is that the human is prevented from his desire, as Allah the Exalted said: 'And a barrier is placed between them and what they desire' {} So this was the most comprehensive expression for the punishments of the people of Hell (Jahannam). And this bliss is attained by the martyr as his soul (Nafs) is cut off without delay. And this matter is revealed to the possessors of hearts (Arbab al-Qulub) by the light (Nur) of certainty (Yaqin). And if you want testimony for it from the side of hearing (Sam'), then all the narrations (Ahadith) of the martyrs indicate it, and every narration that encompasses expressing the ultimate of their bliss with another expression, for it has been narrated from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that he", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Insight"}], "7": [{"arabic": "فإنه عمل في الباطن بالصبر المجرد. والثاني أنه قهر لعدو الله عز وجل فإن وسيلة الشيطان لعنه الله الشهوات وإنما تقوى الشهوات بالأكل والشرب ولذلك قال ﭬ: (إن الشيطان ليجري من ابن آدم مجرى الدم فضيقوا مجاريه بالجوع[12]) ولذلك قال ﭬ لعائشة رضي الله عنها: (داومي قرع باب الجنة قالت: بماذا؟ قال ﭬ بالجوع[13]) وسيأتي فضل الجوع في كتاب شره الطعام وعلاجه من ربع المهلكات فلما كان الصوم على الخصوص قمعا للشيطان وسدا لمسالكه وتضييقا لمجاريه استحق التخصيص بالنسبة إلى الله عز وجل ففي قمع عدو الله نصرة لله سبحانه ون", "english": "For it is an action in the inner realm (Batin) through pure patience (Sabr). The second is that it is a subduing of the enemy of Allah, the Exalted, for the means of Satan, may Allah curse him, are the desires (Shahawat), and the desires are only strengthened by eating and drinking. Therefore, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: 'Indeed, Satan flows in the son of Adam like blood, so constrict his pathways with hunger.' And therefore, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said to Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: 'Persist in knocking on the door of Paradise.' She said: 'With what?' He said: 'With hunger.' And the virtue of hunger will come in the book on the greed for food and its treatment from the quarter of the destructive matters. Since fasting, in particular, is a suppression of Satan, a blocking of his paths, and a constriction of his channels, it deserves specification in relation to Allah, the Exalted. For in suppressing the enemy of Allah, there is victory for Allah, the Glorified, and the supporter of Allah, the Exalted, is dependent on victory for Him. Allah, the Exalted, said: 'If you support Allah, He will support you and make firm your feet.' So the beginning is with effort from the servant (Abd), and the recompense is with guidance from Allah, the Exalted. And therefore, He, the Exalted, said: 'And those who strive in Us, We will surely guide them to Our ways.' And He, the Exalted, said: 'Indeed, Allah does not change the condition of a people until they change what is in their souls (Anfus).' And the change is only the increase of desires, for they are the pasture of the devils (Shayatin) and their grazing ground. As long as they are fertile, their frequenting does not cease, and as long as they frequent, the majesty of Allah, the Glorified, is not unveiled to the servant, and he remains veiled from meeting Him. And the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: 'Were it not that the devils hover over the hearts (Qulub) of the children of Adam, they would look at the dominion of the heavens.' From this perspective, fasting became the gate of worship and became a shield, and since its virtue has reached this extent, it is necessary to clarify its apparent and hidden conditions by mentioning its pillars, its recommended practices, and its hidden conditions, and we will explain that in three chapters.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Fasting", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Mysteries of Fasting'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وقال كعب الأحبار ما في القرآن من يا أيها الذين آمنوا فهو في التوراة يا أيها المساكين", "english": "And Ka'b al-Ahbar said: 'What is in the Quran of \"O you who have believed\" is in the Torah \"O you poor ones (al-Masakin)\".'", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k05.doc.txt", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "General"}], "12": [{"arabic": "وطائفة أخرى زعموا أنهم تفطنوا الأمر وهو أنه ليس المقصود أن يشقى الإنسان بالعمل ولا يتنعم في الدنيا؛ بل السعادة في أن يقضي وطره من شهوة الدنيا وهي شهوة البطن والفرج، فهؤلاء نسوا أنفسهم وصرفوا هممهم إلى اتباع النسوان وجمع لذائذ الأطعمة يأكلون كما تأكل الأنعام ويظنون أنهم إذا نالوا ذلك فقد أدركوا غاية السعادة فشغلهم ذلك عن الله تعالى وعن اليوم الآخر.", "english": "And another group claimed that they had discerned the matter, which is that the purpose is not for the human to toil in work nor to indulge in the worldly life; rather, happiness is in satisfying his desire from the worldly desire, which is the desire of the belly and the private parts. These people forgot their own souls (Anfus) and directed their aspirations to following women and gathering pleasures of foods; they eat as the cattle eat, and they think that if they attain that, they have reached the ultimate happiness. So that preoccupied them from Allah the Exalted and from the Last Day.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-6a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of the World", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Condemnation of the World'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "14": [{"arabic": "\"والثانية\" أن يكون قد عرف قبح القبيح، ولكنه لم يتعود العمل الصالح بل زين له سوء عمله فتعاطاه انقياداً لشهواته وإعراضاً عن صواب رأيه لاستيلاء الشهوة عليه، ولكن علم تقصيره في عمله فأمره أصعب من الأول، إذ قد تضاعفت الوظيفة عليه؛ إذ عليه قلع ما رشه في نفسه أولاً من كثرة الاعتياد للفساد، والآخر أن يغرس في نفسه صفة الاعتياد للصلاح ولكنه بالجملة محل قابل للرياضة إن انتهض لها بجد وتشمير وحزم.", "english": "\"The second\" is that he may have recognized the ugliness of the ugly, but he has not accustomed himself to righteous work; rather, his evil work has been adorned for him, so he engaged in it in submission to his desires (Shahawat) and turning away from the correctness of his opinion due to the domination of desire (Shahwa) over him, but he knows his deficiency in his work, so his matter is more difficult than the first, for the duty has multiplied upon him; upon him is to uproot what was implanted in his soul (Nafs) initially from the abundance of habituation to corruption, and the other is to implant in his soul (Nafs) the attribute of habituation to righteousness, but he is, in summary, a place receptive to spiritual discipline (Riyada) if he rises to it with earnestness, exertion, and determination.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book2a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Breaking the Two Desires", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Breaking the Two Desires'", "badge": "Insight"}], "15": [{"arabic": "وقد ذكر الحسن البصري رحمه الله جملتها فقال: إن رمانها مثل الدلاء وإن أنهارها لمن ماء غير آسن وأنهار من لبن لم يتغير طعمه وأنهار من عسل مصفى لم يصفه الرجال وأنها من خمر لذة للشاربين لا تسفه الأحلام ولا تصدع منها الرءوس", "english": "And Al-Hasan Al-Basri, may Allah have mercy upon him, mentioned its entirety and said: 'Indeed its pomegranates are like buckets, and indeed its rivers are of water not stagnant (ghayr āsin), and rivers of milk whose taste has not changed (lam yataghayyar taʿmuhu), and rivers of purified honey (ʿasal muṣaffan) which men have not purified, and it is of wine (khamr) a delight (ladhdha) for the drinkers, which does not befuddle the minds (lā tusfihu al-aḥlām) nor cause headaches from it (lā taṣdaʿu minhā al-ruʾūs).'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Dhikr"}, {"arabic": "ام ذى غصة فيذكرون كما كانوا يجيزون الغصص فى الدنيا بشراب فيستغيثون بشراب فيرفع إليهم الحميم بكلاليب الحديد فإذا دنت من وجوههم شوت وجوههم فإذا دخل الشراب بطونهم قطع ما فى بطونهم فيقولون ادعوا خزنة جهنم قال فيدعون خزنة جهنم أن ادعوا ربكم يخفف عنا يوما من العذاب فيقولون أو لم تك تأتيكم رسلكم بالبينات قالوا بلى قالوا فادعوا وما دعاء الكافرين إلا فى ضلال قال فيقولون ادعوا مالكا فيدعون فيقولون يا مالك ليقض علينا ربك قال فيجيبهم إنكم ماكثون[205]) قال الأعمش أنبئت أن بين دعائهم وبين إجابة مالك إياهم ألف", "english": "Or one with a choking (ghussa) - they remember as they used to pass through chokings in the world with drink, so they call for help with drink, and the scalding water (al-hamim) is raised to them with iron hooks. When it approaches their faces, it scorches their faces, and when the drink enters their bellies, it cuts what is in their bellies. They say: Call the keepers of Hell. He said: So they call the keepers of Hell: Call your Lord to lighten for us a day of the punishment. They say: Did not your messengers come to you with clear proofs? They say: Yes. They say: Then call, and the call of the disbelievers is only in error. He said: So they say: Call Malik. So they call, and they say: O Malik, let your Lord decide upon us. He said: So He answers them: You will remain. [205] Al-A'mash said: I was informed that between their call and Malik's answer to them is a thousand years. He said: So they say: Call your Lord, for no one is better than your Lord. They say: Our Lord, our wretchedness has overcome us, and we were a people astray. Our Lord, bring us out of it; if we return, then indeed we are wrongdoers. He said: So He answers them: Be driven into it and do not speak. He said: So at that, they despair of every good, and at that, they begin sighing and regret and woe. And Abu Umamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said regarding His saying, the Exalted: 'And he will be given drink from purulent water, which he will gulp and can hardly swallow' [Quran 14:16-17] - He said: It is brought near to him, and he dislikes it, and when it is brought near to him, it scorches his face, and the skin of his head falls off, and when he drinks it, it cuts his intestines until it exits from his anus. Allah, the Exalted, says: 'And they will be given drink scalding water that will cut their intestines' [Quran 47:15]. And He, the Exalted, says: 'And if they call for relief, they will be relieved with water like molten brass that will scald the faces' [Quran 18:29]. So this is their food and drink when they are hungry and thirsty. [206] Then look now at the snakes of Hell and its scorpions, and at the intensity of its poisonous winds and the greatness of its figures and the harshness of its appearance, and it has been given authority over its people and incited against them, so it does not cease from biting and stinging for a single hour. Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever Allah gives wealth and he does not pay its Zakat (obligatory alms), it will be made to appear to him on the Day of Resurrection as a bald snake with two fangs that will encircle him on the Day of Resurrection, then it will take by its cheek, meaning its flanks, and say: I am your wealth, I am your treasure. Then he recited His saying, the Exalted: 'And let not those who are stingy with what Allah has given them of His bounty think' [Quran 3:180] the verse. [207] And the Messenger (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, in the Fire are snakes like the necks of Bactrian camels that sting a sting, and one finds its heat for forty autumns, and indeed in it are scorpions like mules with loads that sting a sting, and one finds its heat for forty autumns. And these snakes and scorpions are only given authority over those who were given authority in the world over stinginess and bad character and harming people, and whoever is protected from that is protected from these snakes, so they do not appear to him. [208] Then reflect after all this on the magnification of the bodies of the people of the Fire, for Allah, the Exalted, increases in their bodies length and width until their punishment increases because of it, and they feel the scorching of the Fire and the stinging of the scorpions and snakes from all.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "16": [{"arabic": "ومن لم يكن له فهم ما في القرآن ولو في أدنى الدرجات دخل في قوله تعالى: ﴿ ومنهم من يستمع إليك حتى إذا خرجوا من عندك قالوا للذين أوتوا العلم ماذا قال آنفا أولئك الذين طبع الله على قلوبهم ﴾ والطابع هي الموانع التي سنذكرها في موانع الفهم وقد قيل: لا يكون المريد مريدا حتى يجد في القرآن كل ما يريد ويعرف منه النقصان من المزيد ويستغني بالمولى عن العبيد.", "english": "And whoever does not have understanding of what is in the Quran, even in the lowest degrees, enters into His saying, the Exalted: 'And among them are those who listen to you until when they depart from your presence, they say to those who were given knowledge: What did he say just now? Those are the ones upon whose hearts Allah has set a seal.' And the seal (Taba') are the obstacles that we will mention in the obstacles of understanding. And it has been said: The Seeker (Murid) does not become a true seeker until he finds in the Quran everything he desires and recognizes from it the deficiency from the increase and becomes independent with the Master (Mawla) from the servants.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "17": [{"arabic": "والهداية الثانية وراء هذه الهداية العامة وهى التى يمد الله تعالى بها العبد حالا بعد حال وهى ثمرة المجاهدة حيث قال تعالى: ﴿ والذين جاهدوا فينا لنهدينهم سبلنا ﴾ {} وهو المراد بقوله تعالى: ﴿ والذين اهتدوا زادهم هدى ﴾ {} والهداية الثالثة وراء الثانية وهو النور الذى يشرق في عالم النبوة والولاية بعد كمال المجاهدة فيهتدى بها إلا ما لا يهتدى إليه بالعقل الذى يحصل به التكليف وإمكان تعلم العلوم وهو الهوى المطلق وما عداه حجاب له ومقدمات وهو الذى شرفه الله تعالى بتخصيص الإضافة إليه وإن كان الكل من جهته تعال", "english": "And the second guidance is beyond this general guidance, and it is that which Allah the Exalted provides to the servant state after state, and it is the fruit of striving (Mujahadah) where He the Exalted said: 'And those who strive in Us, We will surely guide them to Our ways' (29:69). And it is what is intended by His the Exalted saying: 'And those who are guided, He increases them in guidance' (47:17). And the third guidance is beyond the second, and it is the light (Nur) that shines in the world of prophethood (Nubuwwah) and sainthood (Wilayah) after the perfection of striving (Mujahadah), so one is guided by it except what cannot be guided to by the intellect (Aql) through which obligation (Taklif) and the possibility of learning sciences is attained, and it is the absolute desire (Hawa al-Mutlaq), and what is besides it is a veil (Hijab) for it and preliminaries, and it is that which Allah the Exalted honored by specifying the attribution to Him, even though all is from His side the Exalted, so He the Exalted said: 'Say, Indeed, the guidance of Allah is the guidance' (6:71). And it is named life (Hayat) in His the Exalted saying: 'Or one who was dead and We gave him life and made for him a light (Nur) by which he walks among the people' (6:122). And the meaning in His the Exalted saying: 'So is one whose breast Allah has expanded to Islam, then he is upon a light (Nur) from his Lord' (39:22).", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}], "19": [{"arabic": "وذكر ذلك مطلقا في مواضع الترغيب ثم ذكر في بعض المواضع الترغيب ثم ذكر في بعض المواضع الصدق والإخلاص فقال مرة من قال لا إله إلا الله مخلصا ومعنى الإخلاص مساعدة الحال للمقال. فنسأل الله تعالى أن يجعلنا في الخاتمة من أهل لا إله إلا الله حالا ومقالا ظاهرا وباطنا حتى نودع الدنيا غير متلفتين إليها بل متبرمين بها ومحبين للقاء الله فإن من أحب لقاء الله تعالى أحب الله لقاءه ومن كره لقاء الله كره الله لقاءه فهذه مرامز إلى معاني الذكر التي لا يمكن الزيادة عليها في علم المعاملة. (الباب الثاني في آداب الدعاء ", "english": "And he mentioned that absolutely in places of encouragement, then he mentioned in some places of encouragement, then he mentioned in some places sincerity (Sidq) and devotion (Ikhlas), saying once: 'Whoever says \"There is no god but Allah\" with devotion (Ikhlas),' and the meaning of devotion (Ikhlas) is the state (Hal) assisting the statement (Maqal). So we ask Allah the Exalted to make us in the conclusion among the people of \"There is no god but Allah\" in state (Hal) and statement (Maqal), outwardly and inwardly, until we bid farewell to the world not turning towards it but rather weary of it and loving the meeting with Allah. For whoever loves the meeting with Allah the Exalted, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. These are indicators to the meanings of the Remembrance (Dhikr) that cannot be increased upon in the knowledge of interaction. (The Second Chapter on the Etiquettes of Supplication and Its Virtue and the Virtue of Some Transmitted Supplications and the Virtue of Seeking Forgiveness and Prayers upon the Messenger of Allah ﭬ) (The Virtue of Supplication) Allah the Exalted said: 'And when My servants ask you concerning Me, indeed I am near. I respond to the invocation of the supplicant when he calls upon Me.' {} And He said: 'Invoke your Lord in humility and secretly; indeed, He does not like transgressors.' {} And", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ومثل هذا الشخص هو البائع للدنيا بالآخرة وحالة الشهيد توافق معنى قولك لا إله إلا الله فإنه لا مقصود له سوى الله عز وجل وكل مقصود معبود وكل معبود إله فهذا الشهيد قائل بلسان حاله لا إله إلا الله إذ لا مقصود له سواه ومن يقول ذلك بلسانه ولم يساعده حاله فأمره في مشيئة الله عز وجل ولا يؤمن في حقه الخطر ولذلك فضل رسول الله ﭬ قول لا إله إلا الله على سائر الأذكار وذكر ذلك مطلقا في مواضع الترغيب ثم ذكر في بعض المواضع الصدق والإخلاص فقال مرة من قال لا إله إلا الله مخلصا ومعنى الإخلاص مساعدة الحال للمقال. فن", "english": "And such a person is the seller of the worldly life (Dunya) for the Hereafter (Akhirah), and the state of the martyr (Shahid) corresponds to the meaning of your saying 'There is no god but Allah' (La ilaha illa Allah), for he has no objective (Maqsud) except Allah the Exalted, and every objective is worshipped (Ma'bud), and every worshipped one is a god (Ilah). So this martyr is saying with the tongue of his state (Lisan al-Hal) 'There is no god but Allah', since he has no objective other than Him. And whoever says that with his tongue but his state (Hal) does not assist his statement (Maqal), his affair is in the will (Mashiyyah) of Allah the Exalted, and danger (Khatar) is not secured in his right. And for that reason, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) preferred the saying 'There is no god but Allah' over all other remembrances (Adhkar), and he mentioned that absolutely in places of encouragement (Targhib). Then he mentioned in some places sincerity (Sidq) and purity of intention (Ikhlas), saying once: 'Whoever says \"There is no god but Allah\" with purity of intention (Mukhlisan).' And the meaning of purity of intention (Ikhlas) is the assistance of the state (Hal) to the statement (Maqal). So we ask Allah the Exalted to make us in the ending (Khatimah) among the people of 'There is no god but Allah' in state (Hal) and statement (Maqal), outwardly (Zahiran) and inwardly (Batinan), until we bid farewell to the worldly life (Dunya) not turning back to it, but rather being weary of it and loving the meeting (Liqa') with Allah. For whoever loves the meeting with Allah the Exalted, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. These are indications (Maramiz) to the meanings of the remembrance (Dhikr) that cannot be increased upon in the science of interaction (Ilm al-Mu'amalah). (Chapter Two on the Etiquettes of Supplication (Adab al-Du'a) and its virtue and the virtue of some transmitted supplications and the virtue of seeking forgiveness (Istighfar) and sending prayers upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)) (The Virtue of Supplication (Fadilat al-Du'a)) Allah the Exalted said: 'And when My servants ask you concerning Me, indeed I am near. I respond to the invocation of the supplicant when he calls upon Me. So let them respond to Me and believe in Me that they may be guided.' And He said: 'So know that there is no god but Allah and ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women. And Allah knows your movements and your resting place.'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وأما الآثار؛ فقد جاء في الأثر: لا تزال لا إله إلا الله تدفع عن العباد سخط الله عز وجل ما لم يسألوا ما نقص من دنياهم. وفي لفظ آخر: ما لم يؤثروا صفقة دنياهم على دينهم، فإذا فعلوا ذلك وقالوا: لا إله إلا الله، قال الله تعالى: كذبتم، لستم بها صادقين.", "english": "As for the narrations; it has come in a narration: 'There is no god but Allah' continues to repel from the servants the wrath of Allah the Exalted as long as they do not ask for what diminishes from their worldly life. And in another wording: as long as they do not prefer the transaction of their worldly life over their religion, so if they do that and say: 'There is no god but Allah', Allah the Exalted says: 'You have lied, you are not truthful in it.'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "توضع في ميزان لأنها لو وضعت في ميزان من قالها صادقا ووضعت السموات السبع والأرضون السبع وما فيهن كان لا إله إلا الله أرجح من ذلك[22]) وقال ﭬ: (لو جاء قائل لا إله إلا الله صادقا بقراب الأرض ذنوبا لغفر الله له ذلك[23]) وقال ﭬ: (يا أبا هريرة لقن الموتي شهادة أن لا إله إلا الله فإنها تهدم الذنوب هدما. قلت: يا رسول الله هذا للموتي فكيف للأحياء؟ قال ﭬ: هي أهدم وأهدم[24]) وقال ﭬ: (من قال لا إله إلا الله مخلصا دخل الجنة[25]) وقال ﭬ : (لتدخلن الجنة كلكم إلا من أبى وشرد عن الله عز وجل شراد البعير عن أهله. ", "english": "It is placed in the scale because if it were placed in the scale of one who says it truthfully and the seven heavens and the seven earths and what is in them were placed, 'There is no god but Allah' would outweigh that [22]. And he (peace be upon him) said: (If a person comes saying 'There is no god but Allah' truthfully with sins as much as the earth, Allah would forgive him that [23]). And he (peace be upon him) said: (O Abu Hurairah, teach the dead the testimony that there is no god but Allah, for it demolishes sins completely. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for the dead, so how about for the living? He (peace be upon him) said: It is more demolishing and more demolishing [24]). And he (peace be upon him) said: (Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' sincerely enters Paradise [25]). And he (peace be upon him) said: (You will all enter Paradise except whoever refuses and strays from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, like the straying of a camel from its people. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the one who refuses and strays from Allah? He said: Whoever does not say 'There is no god but Allah' [26], so increase in saying 'There is no god but Allah' before a barrier is placed between you and it, for it is the word of Monotheism (Tawhid) and it is the word of Sincerity (Ikhlas) and it is the word of Piety (Taqwa) and it is a good word and it is the call of truth and it is the firmest handhold and it is the price of Paradise). And Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: {Is the reward for good [anything] but good?} {} It was said: The good in this world is saying 'There is no god but Allah' and in the Hereafter is Paradise. And likewise His saying, the Exalted: {For those who do good is the best [reward] and extra} {}. And Al-Bara' ibn 'Azib narrated that he (peace be upon him) said: (Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent' ten times, it will be for him equal to freeing a neck or he said a soul [27]). And 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated from his father from his grandfather that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: (Whoever says in a day two hundred times 'There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent', no one before him will precede him and no one after him will catch him except whoever acts with better than his action [28]). And he (peace be upon him) said: (Whoever says in a market from the markets 'There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things competent', Allah writes for him a thousand thousand good deeds and erases from him a thousand thousand bad deeds and builds for him a house in Paradise). And it is narrated: (Indeed, when the servant (Abd) says 'There is no god but Allah', it comes to his record and does not pass by a sin except it erases it until it finds a good deed like it and sits next to it [29]). And in the authentic from Ayyub from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: (Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent' ten times, it is as if he freed four persons from the children of Ishmael (peace be upon him) [30]). And in the authentic also from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: (Whoever wakes up from the night and says 'There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter", "badge": "Afterlife"}, {"arabic": "فر الله له ذلك[23]) وقال ﭬ: (يا أبا هريرة لقن الموتي شهادة أن لا إله إلا الله فإنها تهدم الذنوب هدما. قلت: يا رسول الله هذا للموتي فكيف للأحياء؟ قال ﭬ: هي أهدم وأهدم[24]) وقال ﭬ: (من قال لا إله إلا الله مخلصا دخل الجنة[25]) وقال ﭬ : (لتدخلن الجنة كلكم إلا من أبى وشرد عن الله عز وجل شراد البعير عن أهله. فقيل: يا رسول الله من الذي يأبى ويشرد عن الله؟ قال: من لم يقل لا إله إلا الله [26]، فأكثروا من قول لا إله إلا الله قبل أن يحال بينكم وبينها فإنها كلمة التوحيد وهي كلمة الإخلاص وهي كلمة التقوى وهي ", "english": "So Allah forgave him that[23]) and He (the Prophet) said: (O Abu Huraira, teach the dying the testimony that there is no god but Allah, for it demolishes sins completely. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for the dying, so how about for the living? He said: It is more demolishing and more demolishing[24]) and He said: (Whoever says there is no god but Allah sincerely enters Paradise[25]) and He said: (You will all enter Paradise except whoever refuses and flees from Allah the Almighty like the camel flees from its owner. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the one who refuses and flees from Allah? He said: Whoever does not say there is no god but Allah [26], so increase in saying there is no god but Allah before a barrier is placed between you and it, for it is the word of Monotheism (Tawhid) and it is the word of Sincerity (Ikhlas) and it is the word of Piety (Taqwa) and it is a good word and it is the call of Truth and it is the firmest handhold and it is the price of Paradise). And Allah the Almighty said: 'Is the reward for good (Ihsan) anything but good (Ihsan)?' {} It was said: The good (Ihsan) in this world is saying there is no god but Allah and in the Hereafter is Paradise. And likewise His saying the Exalted: 'For those who do good (Ahsanu) is the best reward and an increase' {} and Al-Bara' ibn 'Azib narrated that He said: (Whoever says there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent ten times, it will be for him equal to freeing a neck or he said a soul[27]) and 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated from his father from his grandfather that he said: The Messenger of Allah said: (Whoever says in a day two hundred times there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent, no one before him will precede him and no one after him will catch up to him except whoever acts with better than his action[28]) and He said: (Whoever says in a market from the markets there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, He gives life and causes death and He is over all things competent, Allah writes for him a thousand thousand good deeds and erases from him a thousand thousand bad deeds and builds for him a house in Paradise) and it is narrated: (Indeed the servant when he says there is no god but Allah, it comes to his record and does not pass by a sin except it erases it until it finds a good deed like it and sits beside it[29]) and in the authentic from Ayyub from the Prophet that he said: (Whoever says there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent ten times, he is like whoever freed four persons from the children of Ishmael[30]) and in the authentic also from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet that he said: (Whoever wakes up from the night and says there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent, glory be to Allah and praise be to Allah and there is no god but Allah and Allah is greater and there is no power and no strength except with Allah the Most High the Most Great then says O Allah forgive me, he is forgiven or he supplicates, he is answered, then if he performs ablution and prays, his prayer is accepted[31]). (Virtue", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance", "badge": "Du'a"}], "22": [{"arabic": "وأوصي المهاجرين فيما بينهم فإن الله عز وجلّ قال: ﴿ والعصر إن الإنسان لفي خسر إلا الذين آمنوا ﴾{} إلى آخرها وإن الأمور تجري بإذن الله فلا يحملنكم استبطاء أمر على استعجاله فإن الله عز وجل لا يعجل لعجلة أحد ومن غالب الله غلبه ومن خادع الله خدعه ﴿ فهل عسيتم إن توليتم أن تفسدوا في الأرض وتقطعوا أرحامكم ﴾{} وأوصيكم بالأنصار خيرا فإنهم الذين تبوءوا الدار والإيمان من قبلكم أن تحسنوا إليهم ألم يشاطروكم الثمار ألم يوسعوا عليكم في الديار ألم يؤثروكم على أنفسهم وبهم الخصاصة ألا فمن ولي أن يحكم بين رجلين فلي", "english": "And I advise the Emigrants (Muhajirun) among themselves, for Allah the Exalted said: 'By time, indeed, mankind is in loss, except for those who have believed...' to its end. And matters proceed by the permission of Allah, so do not let the delay of a matter lead you to hasten it, for Allah the Exalted does not hasten due to anyone's haste. And whoever contends with Allah, He overcomes him, and whoever deceives Allah, He deceives him. 'Then, would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth and sever your [ties of] kinship?' And I advise you regarding the Helpers (Ansar) with goodness, for they are those who settled the Home and Faith before you, that you treat them well. Did they not share the fruits with you? Did they not make room for you in the dwellings? Did they not prefer you over themselves while they were in need? Indeed, whoever is appointed to judge between two men, let him accept from their doer of good and overlook their wrongdoer. Indeed, and do not monopolize over them. Indeed, I am a forerunner for you, and you will follow me. Indeed, your appointment is the Pool—my Pool is wider than what is between Busra in Syria and Sana'a in Yemen—into which pours the spout of Al-Kawthar. Its water is whiter than milk, softer than foam, and sweeter than honey. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst again. Its pebbles are pearls, and its ground is musk. Whoever is deprived of it on the Day of Standing (Yawm al-Qiyamah) tomorrow is deprived of all good. Indeed, whoever loves to meet me tomorrow, let him restrain his tongue and hand except from what is appropriate.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Insight"}], "31": [{"arabic": "وكان الفضيل بن عياض إذا قرأ (ولنبلونكم حتى نعلم المجاهدين منكم والصابرين ونبلو أخباركم) يبكي ويرددها ويقول إنك إن بلوتنا فضحتنا وهتكت أستارنا.", "english": "And Fudayl ibn Iyad, when he recited (And We will surely test you until We know those who strive among you and those who are patient, and We will test your reports), would weep and repeat it, saying: 'If You test us, You expose us and tear our veils.'", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k07-old.doc.txt", "book_title": "Intention, Sincerity and Truthfulness", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Intention, Sincerity and Truthfulness'", "badge": "General"}], "33": [{"arabic": "وقال كعب الأحبار ما في القرآن من يا أيها الذين آمنوا فهو في التوراة يا أيها المساكين", "english": "And Ka'b al-Ahbar said: 'What is in the Quran of \"O you who have believed\" is in the Torah \"O you poor ones (al-Masakin)\".'", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k05.doc.txt", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "General"}], "36": [{"arabic": "ثم رده تعالى في موضع آخر إلى اثنين فقال تعالى: \" وإنما الحياة الدنيا لعب ولهو \" ثم رد الكل إلى واحد في موضع آخر فقال: \" ونهى النفس عن الهوى فإن الجنة هي المأوى \" فالهوى لفظ يجمع جميع حظوظ النفس في الدنيا، فينبغي أن يكون الزهد فيه.", "english": "Then He (Exalted) reduced it in another place to two, saying (Exalted): \"And indeed the life of the world is play and amusement.\" Then He reduced the whole to one in another place, saying: \"And restrain the Soul (Nafs) from desire (Hawa), for indeed Paradise is the abode.\" So desire (Hawa) is a term that gathers all the shares/portions (Huzuz) of the Soul (Nafs) in the world, therefore asceticism (Zuhd) should be in it.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Insight"}], "37": [{"arabic": "وقد أشار القرآن إليه إذ قال تعالى: ﴿ إن يسألكموها فيحفكم تبخلوا ﴾ {} بل الحق الذى لا كدورة فيه والعدل الذى لا ظلم فيه أن لا يأخذ أحد من عباد الله من مال الله إلا بقدر زاد الراكب فكل عباد الله ركاب لمطايا الأبدان إلى حضرة الملك الديان. فمن أخذ زيادة عليه ثم منعه عن راكب آخر محتاج إليه فهو ظالم تارك للعدو وخارج عن مقصود الحكمة وكافر نعمة الله تعالى عليه بالقرآن والرسول والعقل وسائر الأسباب التى بها عرف ان ما سوى زاد الراكب وبال عليه في الدنيا والآخرة", "english": "And the Quran has indicated to it when He, the Exalted, said: 'If He were to ask you for it and press you, you would withhold and your grudges would emerge' (Quran 47:37). Rather, the truth (Haqq) that has no turbidity in it and the justice (Adl) that has no oppression (Zulm) in it is that no one from the servants (Ibad) of Allah takes from the wealth (Mal) of Allah except according to the measure of the provision of the traveler (Zad al-Rakib). For all the servants (Ibad) of Allah are travelers (Rukab) on the mounts of the bodies (Abdan) to the presence (Hudur) of the King (Malik), the Judge (Dayyan). So whoever takes an increase beyond that, then prevents it from another traveler (Rakib) who is in need of it, he is an oppressor (Zalim), abandoning justice (Adl), and outside the intended wisdom (Hikmah), and ungrateful (Kafir) for the blessing (Nimah) of Allah, the Exalted, upon him through the Quran, the Messenger, the intellect (Aql), and all the other means through which he knew that whatever is beyond the provision of the traveler (Zad al-Rakib) is a burden upon him in this world (Dunya) and the hereafter (Akhirah).", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "القسم الثالث الذين يقتصرون على أداء الواجب فلا يزيدون عليه ولا ينقصون عنه وهي أقل الرتب وقد اقتصر جميع العوام عليه لبخلهم بالمال وميلهم إليه وضعف حبهم للآخرة قال الله تعالى: ﴿ إن يسألكموها فيحفكم تبخلوا ﴾ {} يحفكم أي يستقصّ عليكم فكم بين عبد اشترى منه ماله ونفسه بأن له الجنة وبين عبد لا يستقصى عليه لبخله فهذا أحد معاني أمر الله سبحانه عبادة ببذل الأموال. المعنى الثاني التطهير من صفة البخل فإنه من المهلكات قال ﭬ: (ثلاث مهلكات شح مطاع وهوى متبع وإعجاب المرء بنفسه[9]) وقال تعالى: ﴿ ومن يوق شح نفسه ", "english": "The third category: those who limit themselves to performing the obligatory duty, neither increasing upon it nor decreasing from it, and this is the lowest rank. All common people have limited themselves to this due to their stinginess with wealth, their inclination toward it, and their weak love for the Hereafter. Allah the Exalted said: 'If He were to ask you for it and press you, you would withhold and He would expose your grudges.' {} 'Yuhfikum' means He would exact it from you completely. How great is the difference between a servant from whom his wealth and his soul were purchased in exchange for Paradise, and a servant who is not exacted from due to his stinginess. This is one of the meanings of Allah's command to worship Him by spending wealth. The second meaning: purification from the attribute of stinginess, for it is among the destroyers. He (the Prophet) said: 'Three destroyers: obeyed greed, followed desire, and a person's admiration of himself.' And Allah the Exalted said: 'And whoever is protected from the greed (Shuh) of his soul, then those are the successful ones.' {} And it will come in the quarter of the destroyers how it is a destroyer and the method of cleansing from it. The attribute of stinginess only disappears by accustoming oneself to spending wealth, for love of something does not cease except by compelling the soul (Nafs) to abandon it until that becomes habitual. Thus, Zakah in this meaning is a purification (Taharah), meaning it purifies its possessor from the filth of destructive stinginess. Its purification is according to the measure of his spending and according to the measure of his joy in giving it out and his gladness in directing it to Allah the Exalted.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Zakat", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Mysteries of Zakat'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "الثاني شعر الشارب وقد قال ﭬ: (قصوا الشارب) وفي لفظ آخر (جزوا الشوارب) وفي لفظ آخر (حفوا الشوارب وأعفوا اللحى[62]) أي اجعلوها حفاف الشفة أي حولها وحفاف الشيء حوله ومنه ﴿ وترى الملائكة حافين من حول العرش ﴾ {} وفي لفظ آخر احفوا وهذا يشعر بالاستئصال وقوله حفوا يدل على ما دون ذلك وقال الله عز وجل: ﴿ إن يسئلكموها فيحفكم تبخلوا ﴾ {} أي يستقصي عليكم وأما الحلق فلم يرد والإحفاء القريب من الحلق نقل عن الصحابة نظر بعض التابعين إلى رجل أحفى شاربه فقال ذكرتني أصحاب رسول الله ﭬ.", "english": "The second: The hair of the mustache. And He (peace be upon him) said: 'Trim the mustache.' And in another wording: 'Cut the mustaches.' And in another wording: 'Trim the mustaches and let the beards grow.' That is, make them the trimming (hafaf) of the lip, meaning around it, and the trimming (hafaf) of a thing is around it, and from it: 'And you see the angels surrounding (hafeen) from around the Throne.' And in another wording: 'Trim (ahfoo).' And this indicates complete removal, and His saying 'trim (hafoo)' indicates less than that. And Allah the Exalted said: 'If He asks you for it and exhausts (yuhfikum) you, you would withhold.' That is, He would demand from you completely. And as for shaving, it was not mentioned. And the trimming (al-ihfaa) close to shaving was transmitted from the Companions: Some of the Followers looked at a man who trimmed (ahfaa) his mustache and said: 'You reminded me of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-3.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Purity", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Mysteries of Purity'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "38": [{"arabic": "اعلم أن الفقر عبارة عن فقد ما هو محتاج إليه، أما فقد ما لا حاجة إليه فلا يسمى فقراً، وإن كان المحتاج إليه موجوداً مقدوراً عليه لم يكن المحتاج فقيراً، وإذا فهمت هذا لم تشك في أن كل موجود سوى الله تعالى فهو فقير لأنه محتاج إلى دوام الوجود في ثاني الحال ودوام وجود مستفاد من فضل الله تعالى وجوده؛ فإن كان في الوجود موجود ليس وجوده مستفاد له من غيره فهو الغني المطلق، ولا يتصور أن يكون مثل هذا الموجود إلا واحداً، فليس في الوجود إلا غني واحد، وكل من عداه فإنهم محتاجون إليه ليمدوا وجودهم بالدوام، وإلى هذ", "english": "Know that poverty (al-faqr) is an expression for the loss of what one is in need of, whereas the loss of what one has no need for is not called poverty. If what is needed exists and is attainable, the one in need is not poor. If you understand this, you will not doubt that every existent besides Allah the Exalted is poor because it is in need of the continuation of existence in the next moment, and the continuation of existence is obtained from the grace of Allah the Exalted for its existence. If there exists in existence an existent whose existence is not obtained from another, then He is the Absolutely Rich (al-Ghani al-Mutlaq), and it is inconceivable that such an existent could be except one. Thus, there is in existence only one Rich (Ghani), and everyone besides Him is in need of Him to extend their existence with continuation. To this exclusivity is the allusion in His saying, the Exalted: \"And Allah is the Rich (al-Ghani) and you are the poor (al-fuqara').\" This is the meaning of poverty absolutely. However, we do not intend to explain absolute poverty but poverty from wealth in particular, otherwise the poverty of the servant (al-'abd) in relation to the varieties of his needs is not limited, because his needs are without limit.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 1737], [2, 1737, 3180], [3, 3180, 4990], [4, 4990, 5511], [5, 5511, 6599], [6, 6599, 7534], [7, 7534, 8540], [8, 8540, 10172]], "2": [[1, 400, 2048], [2, 2048, 3777], [3, 3777, 5575], [4, 5575, 7581], [5, 7581, 9656], [6, 9656, 10486], [7, 10486, 11351], [8, 11351, 12411], [9, 12411, 13690], [10, 13690, 14589], [11, 14589, 15626], [12, 15626, 16087], [13, 16087, 17332], [14, 17332, 18197], [15, 18197, 19142], [16, 19142, 21107], [17, 21107, 22513], [18, 22513, 23782]], "3": [[1, 400, 1354], [2, 1354, 2534], [3, 2534, 3968], [4, 3968, 5516], [5, 5516, 7382], [6, 7382, 8702], [7, 8702, 10009], [8, 1000